Input: {"question": "In which state is the Haymarket District located?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0422-d0124ba1bc0f:d00", "start": 0, "end": 178, "text": "Haymarket District (Lincoln, Nebraska) \"For other subjects known by a similar name see Haymarket District\" Haymarket District is a historic section of downtown Lincoln, Nebraska."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0422-d0124ba1bc0f:d00", "start": 179, "end": 212, "text": "The area is a tourist attraction."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0422-d0124ba1bc0f:d00", "start": 213, "end": 269, "text": "The area is home to the Haymarket Park baseball stadium."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0422-d0124ba1bc0f:d00", "start": 270, "end": 371, "text": "The name Haymarket originated from the 1867 market square where hay, and travel items, were marketed."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0422-d0124ba1bc0f:d00", "start": 372, "end": 423, "text": "The warehouses have been readapted as retail shops."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0422-d0124ba1bc0f:d00", "start": 424, "end": 439, "text": "The historic J."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0422-d0124ba1bc0f:d00", "start": 440, "end": 442, "text": "C."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0422-d0124ba1bc0f:d00", "start": 443, "end": 522, "text": "Ridnour Building (1925) designed by Meginnis and Schaumberg is in the district."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0422-d0124ba1bc0f:d00", "start": 523, "end": 567, "text": "The district held a Halloween event in 2018."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0422-d0124ba1bc0f:d00", "start": 568, "end": 640, "text": "Buildings in the district were designed by various firms oncluding Fiske"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0422-d0124ba1bc0f:d01", "start": 0, "end": 611, "text": "Haymarket District ( Lincoln 